                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>"Child and Adolescent Health" is based on the principles of children and adolescents' growth and development, and focuses on the protection, promotion, and enhancement of their physical and mental health. It discusses the determinants of children and adolescents' health and proposes strategies and measures for disease prevention and health intervention. This is a highly practical and applied discipline. The content of the course includes three parts: theories and methods of children and adolescents' growth and development, issues related to their physical and mental health and their prevention and control, as well as school health services and school health promotion.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
